  "term": "heuristic-systematic model",
  "definition": "In cognition, the heuristic-systematic model is a theoretical framework for persuasion proposing that people may rely on source credibility as a heuristic when cognitive elaboration is low, while under higher elaboration the same credibility information can increase scrutiny of the message.",
